---
// Stack frame bump-pointer return (0 GC work) vs heap newobject escape (paid twice: alloc + GC scan).
const W = 900;
const H = 290;
---
<figure class="gesft">
  <div class="gesft-scroll">
    <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Side-by-side trace showing stack pointer unwinding cleanly in 1 CPU instruction versus heap escape calling runtime.newobject and adding Garbage Collector mark/sweep work.">
      {/* Left panel: Stack Allocation Path */}
      <rect x="14" y="14" width="432" height="262" rx="10" class="gesft-card" />
      <text x="30" y="42" class="gesft-h">
        <tspan data-lang-en>1. Stack frame path (no escape = nearly free)</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>1. Cấp phát trên Stack (không escape = gần như miễn phí)</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="30" y="58" width="400" height="58" rx="6" class="gesft-box" />
      <text x="44" y="79" class="gesft-code">func calc() User {'{'} u := User{'{'}ID: 7{'}'}; return u {'}'}</text>
      <text x="44" y="99" class="gesft-m">SUB SP, #frame -&gt; 1 CPU instruction reserves frame</text>

      <rect x="30" y="128" width="400" height="62" rx="6" class="gesft-box is-ok" />
      <text x="44" y="149" class="gesft-b-ok">On return: ADD SP, #frame pops frame instantly</text>
      <text x="44" y="168" class="gesft-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>L1-hot memory immediately reused by next function call.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Vùng nhớ nóng sẵn trên L1 được hàm tiếp theo tái sử dụng ngay.</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="30" y="202" width="400" height="58" rx="6" class="gesft-box is-ok" />
      <text x="44" y="223" class="gesft-b-ok">Garbage Collector cost: ZERO (0 scans, 0 barriers)</text>
      <text x="44" y="242" class="gesft-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Ideal default for temporary values inside hot loops.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Mục tiêu số 1 cho biến tạm nằm trong đường nóng lặp triệu lần.</tspan>
      </text>

      {/* Right panel: Heap Escape Path */}
      <rect x="462" y="14" width="424" height="262" rx="10" class="gesft-card" />
      <text x="478" y="42" class="gesft-h">
        <tspan data-lang-en>2. Heap escape path (pays at allocation AND at GC)</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>2. Thoát lên Heap (trả giá 2 lần: lúc cấp phát &amp; lúc GC dọn)</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="478" y="58" width="392" height="58" rx="6" class="gesft-box is-red" />
      <text x="492" y="79" class="gesft-code">func calcPtr() *User {'{'} u := User{'{'}ID: 7{'}'}; return &amp;u {'}'}</text>
      <text x="492" y="99" class="gesft-b-red">CALL runtime.newobject(type:User) -&gt; heap span lookup</text>

      <rect x="478" y="128" width="392" height="62" rx="6" class="gesft-box" />
      <text x="492" y="149" class="gesft-b">Cost #1: runtime.mallocgc (~20–60 ns + memclr)</text>
      <text x="492" y="168" class="gesft-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>P mcache lookup, zero slot memory, bump GC byte trigger.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Tra mcache kích cỡ, xóa sạch byte, tăng bộ đếm báo GC.</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="478" y="202" width="392" height="58" rx="6" class="gesft-box is-red" />
      <text x="492" y="223" class="gesft-b-red">Cost #2: GC marks pointers &amp; sweeps blocks</text>
      <text x="492" y="242" class="gesft-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>High alloc churn triggers Mark Assist slowing goroutines.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Xả rác nhanh khiến Mark Assist bắt goroutine dọn phụ!</tspan>
      </text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Every variable escaping to the heap triggers both allocation work right now and Garbage Collector tracing later. Keeping small short-lived state on the stack lets Go reclaim memory cleanly with a single stack pointer add.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Mỗi biến thoát lên Heap đều trả tiền 2 lần: tốn công cấp phát từ mcache/mheap ngay bây giờ và tốn CPU đánh dấu dọn dẹp của Garbage Collector về sau. Giữ dữ liệu ngắn hạn trên Stack giải phóng RAM bằng đúng 1 lệnh cộng thanh ghi SP.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .gesft { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .gesft-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .gesft svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 660px; height: auto; }
  .gesft text { font-size: 12px; fill: var(--text-body); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .gesft-card { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .gesft-box { fill: var(--bg); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .gesft-box.is-red { stroke: var(--red); fill: var(--red-tint-bg); }
  .gesft-box.is-ok { stroke: rgb(21, 128, 61); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .gesft-box.is-ok { stroke: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  .gesft-h { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .gesft-b { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .gesft-b-red { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--red); }
  .gesft-b-ok { font-weight: 700; fill: rgb(21, 128, 61); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .gesft-b-ok { fill: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  .gesft-code { font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace); font-size: 10.5px; fill: var(--text); }
  .gesft-m { fill: var(--text-muted); font-size: 10.5px; }
  .gesft figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
